    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The hERG margin is approximately **600-fold**:\n\n`30 \u00b5M / 0.05 \u00b5M = 600`\n\nThat is reassuring for direct hERG-mediated risk, so I would **continue and reasonably prioritise Compound A**, provided the IC50 and free Cmax are measured comparably and there are no other liabilities. It is not, by itself, evidence of overall cardiac or development safety.\n\n**Next study:** run an integrated cardiac safety study, preferably:\n\n- In vivo telemetry with ECG/QTc and blood sampling\n- Exposure at and above the intended free-Cmax range\n- Assessment of active metabolites and relevant exposure multiples\n- Confirmation of hERG findings in a physiologically relevant, concentration-response assay if the original assay was preliminary\n\nA QTc signal, unexpectedly high metabolite exposure, or a substantially lower hERG potency under confirmatory conditions would change the prioritisation.",
